    <string name="bufferbloat_info">Bufferbloat is how much your latency grows when the line is fully loaded — it is what makes calls and games stutter while something is downloading. A and better means the connection stays responsive; C or worse is noticeable. To improve it, enable smart queue management (SQM/QoS with fq_codel or CAKE) on your router and set its bandwidth to about 95 %% of the measured speed.</string>
